.TH EXPIRY-RADAR 1 "2026-09" "expiry-radar" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
expiry-radar \- one inventory of everything that expires, ranked by blast radius
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B expiry-radar
.RI [ flags ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B expiry-radar
collects everything in an estate that has an expiry date \(em TLS certificates,
intermediate CAs, secrets, IAM keys, Vault leases, domains \(em into one report,
ranked by blast radius, so that the certificate on the payment path outranks the
one on a staging dashboard.
.PP
All sources are read-only. The project documentation carries the exact IAM
policy and Kubernetes RBAC Role required.
.PP
Partial failures are reported, never swallowed: if a source fails, the report is
still written, a warning goes to standard error, and the exit status says so.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-config " PATH"
Config file listing the read-only sources to scan (default
.IR expiry-radar.json ).
.TP
.BI \-format " FORMAT"
Output format:
.BR table ", " json ", " ical ", " prometheus ", " html
(default table).
.TP
.BI \-endpoints " HOSTS"
Comma-separated hosts to probe over TLS, in addition to the config.
.TP
.BI \-domains " DOMAINS"
Comma-separated domains to check via RDAP, in addition to the config.
.TP
.BI \-within " N"
Only report items expiring within N days (0 = everything).
.TP
.BI \-fail\-within " N"
Exit 1 if anything expires within N days (0 = never fail).
.TP
.BI \-min\-priority " P"
Only report items at or above this priority.
.TP
.BI \-out " FILE"
Write to a file instead of standard output.
.TP
.BI \-timeout " DURATION"
Overall collection timeout (default 2m).
.TP
.B \-verify\-aws
Run the AWS adapters and report what they did, in a form safe to paste into an
issue (no ARNs, ids or names). This is not a scan.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success; nothing breached the
.B \-fail\-within
window.
.TP
.B 1
Something expires within the
.B \-fail\-within
window.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error, bad config, or the report could not be written.
.TP
.B 3
Results were produced, but at least one source failed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I expiry-radar.json
Default configuration.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Probe two hosts with no config file at all:
.PP
.RS
.B expiry-radar \-endpoints example.com,api.example.com
.RE
.PP
Fail a CI job if anything expires inside a fortnight:
.PP
.RS
.B expiry-radar \-fail\-within 14
.RE
.PP
Scrape it from Prometheus:
.PP
.RS
.B expiry-radar \-format prometheus \-out /var/lib/node_exporter/expiry.prom
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation:
.UR https://github.com/fabiocicerchia/expiry-radar
.UE
